# The database and uploaded files. `crm.db` also holds a verbatim copy of every
# evidence snapshot, so it is both live data and a backup — keep it out of the
# repository, and back it up by copying the file (see backup-db.mjs).
data/

node_modules/
*.log

# Environment files. `.env` was tracked until now, with a live read-write
# database token in it — see the commit that removed it. Nothing reads this
# file (Node does not load it implicitly, and the scripts that need credentials
# take `--env-file=data/turso.env` explicitly), so it was a credential in the
# repository for no working purpose at all.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── local-scraper/ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The qualification rules live in local-scraper/lib, and the CRM reads them
# from there rather than keeping its own copy so the two can never disagree
# about what QUALIFIED means. A deployed CRM has no sibling checkout, so lib/
# is tracked — without it every qualification run fails with "engine not
# found". It is ~100KB of rule modules with no dependencies of their own.
#
# NOTHING else from that project belongs in this repository:
#   browser-profile/   a logged-in browser session — live credentials
#   snapshots.json     scraped evidence, and client data
#   *.csv              prospect and contact lists
#   node_modules/      its dependencies, which the CRM does not share
local-scraper/*
!local-scraper/lib/

# ── Automation/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The templates, the Apps Script sources and the reference drafts ARE tracked:
# the templates are what the CRM generates from, and the drafts are the
# authored documents the regression tests compare against. They were checked
# for client data before being committed and contain none — every party field
# reads "Company Name", "[CLIENT NAME]" or "شركة ………", and the only
# registration number in them is Talent 360's own.
#
# These three are not worth versioning:

# A zip snapshot of apps-script-dms/, which is already tracked as files.
Automation/HCM/apps-script-dms.zip

# Local machine settings, not project configuration.
Automation/HCM/.claude/

# A byte-identical duplicate of "Draft - HCM Agreement  (1).docx" (same md5).
# Safe to delete from the working tree too.
Automation/Draft - HCM Agreement  (1) (1).docx
